  biomeName: Mesa Plateaus
  minDepthMeters: -200
  maxDepthMeters: 0
  shortDescription: Flat-topped dry platforms dotted with giant blue holes full of
    stagnant nutrient-rich water.
  isPlaceholder: 0
  visitPurpose: Early exploration biome. Come here to learn routes, gather basics,
    and work around bowls, pools, and local hotspots.
  commonRewardHook: Common runs pay out in Titanium Scrap and Silica Shards.
  rareRewardHook: 'Rare pull is modest: Fiber Kelp and Glass Panel.'
  landmarkIdentity: Mesa Plateaus reads through bowls, pools, domes, and hotspot
    basins. Landmarks should feel bright and readable.
  safePocketIdentity: Safe pockets are frequent. The player should often see a clear
    reset point nearby.
  riskSummary: 'Main failure mode: localized danger pockets and hostile basins. Creature
    pressure stays low.'
  extractionFocus: 'Loose pickup fields and readable shallow mineral nodes. Early
    tier: keep runs short and expect basin pockets, salvage traps, and local hotspots.'
  landmarkGuidance: Dominant landmark is karst arch or sea-stack crown. This slot
    should read through small limestone teeth and arch feet; use bowls and hotspot
    rims to remember loops.
